            <ArticleTitle>[Factors contributing to the success of intracoronary thrombolytic therapy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>19-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intracoronary thrombolytic therapy (ICT) was used in 36 patients with acute transmural myocardial infarction. Recanalization of an infarction-dependent artery was achieved in 26 (72.2%) patients. Factors affecting the success of ICT were analysed, using Bayes' theorem. The ejection fraction (EF) is shown to have the highest predictive value as an indicator of left-ventricular pump function. The anticipated probability of ICT success is 84.9% in patients with acute myocardial infarction and a 35% EF baseline, and 25.7% in those with a 35% EF. In the absence of severe left-ventricular pumping and contractility disorders, the success of ICT is affected by patient's age, history of myocardial infarction and the site of thrombotic occlusion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
